## Phase 7: CSS Color Parsing & Serialization (W3C Compliance)
### Spec References
- CSS Color Level 4: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-4/
- CSS Color Level 3: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-color-3/

### 7.1 Color Parsing in CssValueParser (CSS/Parser/)
- [x] Handle HashToken → CssValue (COLOR) in Consume_Value()
  - [x] Parse #RGB (3-digit hex)
  - [x] Parse #RGBA (4-digit hex)
  - [x] Parse #RRGGBB (6-digit hex)
  - [x] Parse #RRGGBBAA (8-digit hex)
- [x] Handle rgb()/rgba() function → CssValue (COLOR)
  - [x] Legacy syntax: rgb(255, 128, 0)
  - [x] Modern syntax: rgb(255 128 0)
  - [x] Percentage values: rgb(100%, 50%, 0%)
  - [x] Alpha channel: rgb(255 128 0 / 0.5)
  - [x] CssColorFunctionParser helper class created
  - [x] Tests: 20 tests for rgb/rgba parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle hsl()/hsla() function → CssValue (COLOR)
  - [x] Legacy syntax: hsl(120, 100%, 50%)
  - [x] Modern syntax: hsl(120 100% 50%)
  - [x] Alpha channel: hsl(120 100% 50% / 0.5)
  - [x] Hue angle units: deg, rad, grad, turn
  - [x] HSL to RGB conversion per W3C spec
  - [x] Tests: 20+ tests for hsl/hsla parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle hwb() function → CssValue (COLOR)
  - [x] Modern syntax only: hwb(0 0% 0%) - no legacy comma syntax
  - [x] Whiteness/Blackness: percentage or number (0-100)
  - [x] Alpha channel: hwb(0 0% 0% / 0.5)
  - [x] Hue angle units: deg, rad, grad, turn
  - [x] Achromatic handling when W+B >= 100%
  - [x] HWB to RGB conversion per W3C spec
  - [x] Tests: 23 tests for hwb parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle lab()/lch() functions → CssValue (COLOR)
  - [x] Modern syntax only: lab(L a b) / lch(L C H) - no legacy comma syntax
  - [x] L (Lightness): percentage or number (0-100), clamped to [0,100]
  - [x] a, b (Lab): signed numbers or percentages (-100% to 100% → -125 to 125)
  - [x] C (Chroma): ≥0, percentage maps to 0-150 range
  - [x] H (Hue): angle with deg, rad, grad, turn units
  - [x] Alpha channel: lab(50 40 -30 / 0.5), lch(50 60 180 / 50%)
  - [x] Lab to XYZ to sRGB conversion per W3C CSS Color 4 spec
  - [x] LCH to Lab conversion (polar to cartesian)
  - [x] Gamma correction for sRGB output
  - [x] Tests: 36 tests for lab/lch parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle oklab()/oklch() functions → CssValue (COLOR)
  - [x] Modern syntax only: oklab(L a b) / oklch(L C H) - no legacy comma syntax
  - [x] L (Lightness): percentage or number (0-1), clamped to [0,1]
  - [x] a, b (OKLab): signed numbers or percentages (-100% to 100% → -0.4 to 0.4)
  - [x] C (Chroma): ≥0, percentage maps to 0-0.4 range
  - [x] H (Hue): angle with deg, rad, grad, turn units
  - [x] Alpha channel: oklab(0.5 0.1 -0.1 / 0.5), oklch(0.5 0.15 180 / 50%)
  - [x] OKLab to XYZ to sRGB conversion per W3C CSS Color 4 spec
  - [x] OKLCh to OKLab conversion (polar to cartesian)
  - [x] Tests: 35 tests for oklab/oklch parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle color() function for custom color spaces
  - [x] Modern syntax only: color(<color-space> c1 c2 c3 [/ alpha]) - no legacy comma syntax
  - [x] Predefined RGB color spaces: srgb, srgb-linear, display-p3, a98-rgb, prophoto-rgb, rec2020
  - [x] XYZ color spaces: xyz, xyz-d50, xyz-d65 (xyz is alias for xyz-d65)
  - [x] Component values: number [0-1] or percentage [0%-100%], out-of-gamut allowed
  - [x] Alpha channel: color(srgb 1 0 0 / 0.5), color(display-p3 1 0 0 / 50%)
  - [x] All predefined color space to sRGB conversions implemented
  - [x] EColorSpace enum extended with A98Rgb, ProPhotoRgb, Rec2020, XyzD50, XyzD65
  - [x] Tests: 29 tests for color() parsing (CssColorFunctionParserTests.cs)
- [x] Handle named color keywords (e.g., 'red', 'blue', 'transparent')
  - [x] CSS Color 4 named colors (147 extended colors)
  - [x] 'transparent' keyword → CssColor(0, 0, 0, 0)
  - [x] 'currentColor' keyword → special value
  - [x] TryFromNamedColor method on CssColor for case-insensitive lookup
  - [x] FromEColor factory method for creating colors from EColor enum
  - [x] CssParser integration for parsing IdentToken as named colors
  - [x] Tests: 27 tests for named color parsing (CssNamedColorTests.cs)

### 7.2 Review CSS color parser implementation (CSS/Parser/)
- [x] Ensure compliance with CSS Color 4 spec
  - [x] Fixed: 'none' keyword now correctly rejected in legacy rgb()/hsl() syntax per §4.1.2
- [x] Ensure that parsing follows W3C algorithms exactly
  - [x] Modern vs legacy syntax detection is correct
  - [x] Legacy syntax enforces all-number or all-percentage for RGB components
  - [x] Modern syntax allows freely mixing numbers and percentages
  - [x] HSL saturation clamping to 0 for negative values at parse time
  - [x] HWB, Lab, LCH, OKLab, OKLCh correctly reject legacy comma syntax
  - [x] Extra tokens after expected components now properly rejected
- [x] Ensure that parsing uses the same data types and patterns as the core CssParser
  - [x] Uses CssToken types consistently (NumberToken, PercentageToken, IdentToken, etc.)
  - [x] Returns CssColor values consumed by CssParser.Consume_CssValue()
  - [x] Refactored to use DataConsumer<CssToken> stream pattern for consistency
- [x] Color space conversions verified against W3C spec matrices (Lab, OKLab, Display-P3, etc.)

