### 7.8 CSS Token/Component Value Serialization (CSS/Serialization/)
Spec Reference: https://www.w3.org/TR/css-syntax-3/#serialization

#### 7.8.1 Core Serialization Requirements (§10)
- [ ] Round-trip guarantee: parse → serialize → parse = same result
- [ ] Handle consecutive whitespace tokens (may collapse)
- [ ] Insert comments between tokens that would otherwise merge
  - [ ] Build token adjacency table per spec §10
  - [ ] ident + ident requires separator
  - [ ] number + ident requires separator
  - [ ] etc. (see full table in spec)

#### 7.8.2 Token Serialization
- [ ] Serialize <delim-token> containing \ as \+newline
- [ ] Serialize <hash-token> with proper type flag handling
- [ ] Serialize <dimension-token> unit with escaping for scientific notation ambiguity
- [ ] Serialize all token types to canonical form

#### 7.8.3 Component Value Serialization
